[38;5;231m⏺[39m Codex is installed, but I'm skipping the approach gate: the architectural forks it exists to broaden — destination,
  module format, redaction — are the ones you just decided, so an independent second opinion now would be re-litigating
  settled choices rather than opening new ones. Say so if you'd like it run anyway.

  Here's the design.

  [1mDesign: shared logging module[0m

  [1m1. The module — [38;5;153msrc/logger.js[0m

  One UMD-wrapped file. Node gets it via [38;5;153mrequire('./logger')[39m; the browser gets it from a [38;5;153m<script src="src/logger.js">[39m
  tag added to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, exposing [38;5;153mwindow.logger[39m.

  API:
  logger.debug|info|warn|error(message, context)
  logger.setLevel('debug'|'info'|'warn'|'error')
  logger.setSink(fn)   // the transport seam

  [1m2. The record[0m

  Every call builds one object before anything is emitted:
  { ts: "2026-09-16T12:00:00.000Z", level: "warn", msg: "...", env: "browser"|"node", ctx: {...} }
  [38;5;153menv[39m is there because the whole point of the seam is that browser and Node records eventually land in the same store,
  and you'll want to tell them apart.

  [1m3. Levels[0m

  Ordered [38;5;153mdebug < info < warn < error[39m; anything below the threshold is dropped before redaction or emission. Default

